WEBVTT

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:07.734
Captain's Log,
Stardate 54208.3.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.935
Last month's datastream
from Starfleet never arrived,

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.740
so the crew is looking forward
to this one

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.110
with even more anticipation
than usual.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.706
We could all use some news
from home.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.547
Ah. There he is,
the man of the hour.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.113
You sure are in a good mood.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.749
Well, rumor has it you snared

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.657
the latest datastream
last night.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.423
Technically,
it was this morning...

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:31.623
0200 to be exact.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.427
So where's my mail?

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.933
Hmm?

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.901
Oh. Don't tell me
you lost another one.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.234
I didn't lose
last month's datastream.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.294
It never arrived.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.863
So what's the
holdup this time?

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.432
The transmission was
a little larger than usual.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:45.842
It's jammed
the transceiver.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.641
Seven and I have
been up all night

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:48.840
trying to download it.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:49.973
Harry...

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.075
we can't go another month
without mail.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.414
Oh, you won't.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.646
Trust me.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.259
Any luck?

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:05.126
I've determined why
we've been having difficulties.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.026
A hologram.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.162
The transceiver
wasn't designed

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.933
to store photonic data.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:17.373
We have to get it out of there
before it degrades.

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.105
What are you doing?

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:21.943
Tying the transceiver into
the holodeck's pattern buffer.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.778
Those systems aren't compatible.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.442
You'll depolarize the relays.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.679
Starfleet wouldn't
have sent this hologram

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:28.948
if it weren't important.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.353
I'm sure it's worth
a few burnt-out relays.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.653
You've overloaded
the transceiver.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:40.722
But I saved the hologram.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.838
Okay, ready when you are.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.070
Lieutenant Barclay?

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.806
Uh... no,
but he did design me.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.142
I'm a walking, talking,

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.240
problem-solving
interactive hologram.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.376
You can call me Reg.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.249
It's nice to meet you, Reg.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.583
The pleasure's mine, Captain.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.088
Harry, Seven...

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.318
I've been looking forward
to working with you.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.324
You have?

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.655
I know... you were
expecting letters

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.286
from your friends and families.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.297
But with any luck,
in a few days,

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:15.960
you'll be seeing them
face-to-face.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.510
In three days' time,

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:10.379
Voyager is going to be
passing through Grid 898...

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:14.045
a sector of space occupied
by a red giant star.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.781
Sensors detected it
a few days ago.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:18.153
At this very moment,
a team of Federation scientists

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:21.193
is orbiting another red giant
in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:25.425
In 72 hours, they will target
its magnetic field

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.864
with a verteron beam,

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.765
creating a geodesic fold.

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.737
As a result, a corresponding
fold will open here

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.103
in the magnetic field
of the red giant

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.766
that Voyager is approaching.

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:40.438
Space will be punctured...
these two points

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:43.209
creating a gateway
between the quadrants.

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:46.150
Our shields are useless
against geodesic radiation.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:49.052
We toyed with the idea
of opening a fold ourselves,

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:51.181
but it didn't take us
long to realize

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.918
we wouldn't survive the trip.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.960
A lot's happened
in geodesic research

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.289
since you've been gone.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.660
I've brought schematics
for shield upgrades

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.790
to deflect the radiation
from the fold,

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:02.425
medical technology to provide

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:03.901
additional protection
for the crew.

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:05.231
We've thought of everything.

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:06.636
Starfleet never mentioned you

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.401
in any of the
previous datastreams.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:11.102
Well, Lieutenant Barclay
didn't want to raise your hopes,

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.441
in case the plan didn't
live up to expectation,

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.276
but lucky for you,
it surpassed them.

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:17.612
What about
last month's datastream?

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:19.276
Why didn't we receive it?

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.752
Pathfinder tried sending
an unabridged version

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.083
of my program.

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:24.783
It overloaded the MIDAS Array.

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:27.382
And the only casualty this time
was our transceiver.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.485
If everything goes
according to plan,

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.496
you won't need it anymore.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.498
If we were to attempt this,

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:36.558
you'd need access
to areas of this ship

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.696
that aren't equipped
with holo-emitters.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.399
Not to worry, Captain.

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:43.942
We've thought of that, too.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:47.638
My emitter is your emitter.

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:49.579
Computer, transfer
the Barclay hologram

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.640
to the mobile emitter.

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:53.879
Transfer complete.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.387
On Lieutenant Barclay's
behalf, I thank you.

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:58.890
Just make sure to return
it when we get to Earth.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.791
We're ready for you

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.385
in the briefing room, Captain.

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:05.055
Excuse us, Doctor.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.598
I'm sure you have
a full day planned,

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:07.598
but if you have time,

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.157
I'd like to get
better acquainted.

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:10.725
I'll stop by
the first chance I get.

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.896
You'll know where to find me.

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:14.371
This is our destination...

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.000
Red Giant 23139.

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:19.510
The geodesic fold
will open here,

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:21.479
adjacent to the giant's
northern pole.

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:25.210
We'll have exactly 16 seconds
to take Voyager through.

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.149
Reg has prepared
a list of assignments.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.346
I expect you to give him

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:29.547
your full cooperation.

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:31.021
Mr. Paris, you have the honor

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.853
of plotting our course
to Big Red 2.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.859
Lieutenant Torres,
Commander Tuvok,

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:37.691
I'd like you to start working
on shield modifications.

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:39.664
And in the meantime,
I've asked the Doctor

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:41.256
to prepare a series
of inoculations

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.427
that will protect the
crew from the radiation.

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:44.868
We should discuss
the possibility

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:47.428
of applying Borg technology
to Starfleet's plan.

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:48.701
It could increase

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:50.333
our chances of success.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.503
I look forward
to hearing your thoughts.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.341
How long before
the transceiver's back on line?

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.847
No more than two hours.

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:56.882
Then we'll still have time

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.382
to transmit a
response to Starfleet.

00:06:58.451 --> 00:06:59.884
Keep us posted.

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:01.317
I'd like to send
Lieutenant Barclay

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:03.287
a little thank-you note
for all his hard work.

00:07:04.524 --> 00:07:05.548
Um, uh, is there...

00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:07.422
is there anything I can do, Reg?

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:10.485
Your job might be the
most important one of all.

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.224
The next few days
will be difficult.

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:14.459
The crew will be working
extremely long hours.

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:16.764
They're going to need an
experienced Morale Officer

00:07:16.836 --> 00:07:18.133
to keep their spirits high.

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:19.865
You can count on me.

00:07:21.808 --> 00:07:24.675
If this were any other ship...

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:27.372
I'd have my doubts.

00:07:27.447 --> 00:07:30.348
But this is Voyager,
"the miracle ship."

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:33.908
You've survived six years
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:37.921
You've evaded the Kazon,
the Vidiians, the Hirogen.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.617
You've even faced down the Borg.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:42.525
I think, with a little teamwork,

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:44.620
we can pull off
one more miracle

00:07:44.697 --> 00:07:47.564
and take Voyager home.

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.692
I can taste my
mom's cooking.

00:07:49.769 --> 00:07:52.499
Don't forget what
the hologram said, Harry:

00:07:52.572 --> 00:07:53.937
"This is Voyager...

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:55.405
"The miracle ship"!

00:07:55.475 --> 00:07:57.136
Uh, not when it comes
to getting us home.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:00.441
Our shortcuts have a tendency
to blow up in our faces.

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:02.242
Well, that's looking
on the bright side.

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:04.306
Well, remember Arturis

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:06.476
and his quantum
slipstream drive?

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:10.181
Or, um, or how about
the telepathic pitcher plant

00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:12.053
that made us think
we were on our way home

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:14.319
right before it tried
to eat the ship.

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:15.883
This is the best opportunity
we've had.

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.259
Yeah, which is why

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.457
we'll probably end up
in the Gamma Quadrant.

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:20.829
I'll remind you of that when

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:21.889
we get back to Earth.

00:08:21.968 --> 00:08:22.900
Don't say I didn't warn you.

00:08:22.969 --> 00:08:24.596
When a Borg cube enters

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.501
a transwarp conduit,
it's subject

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.233
to extreme
gravimetric shear.

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:29.433
To compensate, the Borg

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:31.272
project a structural
integrity field

00:08:31.344 --> 00:08:32.811
ahead of the cube.

00:08:32.879 --> 00:08:34.278
By modifying
Voyager's deflector,

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:36.247
we may be able to do the same.

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:38.715
No one at Starfleet
would have thought of this.

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:42.686
So, what's the first thing

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:44.120
you're going to do
when you get back?

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.215
Begin repairs to Voyager.

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:48.123
Even with the structural
integrity field,

00:08:48.194 --> 00:08:50.458
it's likely the ship
will suffer significant damage.

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:53.658
Yes, but, I mean, there are
people at Utopia Planitia

00:08:53.733 --> 00:08:54.700
who will take care of that.

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.325
There are Engineering crews
and technicians...

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:58.632
Are you implying that
I am superfluous?

00:08:58.704 --> 00:09:00.069
Of course not.

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:02.334
I only meant that if
you're too busy working,

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:05.775
you're going to miss all
the "welcome home" hoopla.

00:09:05.845 --> 00:09:07.437
Starfleet's planning parties.

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:09.640
They'll have ceremonies
and speeches.

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:13.776
There, there's a ticker-tape
parade down Market Street.

00:09:13.853 --> 00:09:15.844
I won't be attending
any of those events.

00:09:15.922 --> 00:09:19.119
But you'd be the guest of honor.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.024
When I first arrived
on Voyager,

00:09:23.095 --> 00:09:26.292
it was difficult
for the crew to accept me.

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:28.765
I'm anticipating
a similar welcome on Earth.

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:35.501
You don't have
any idea, do you?

00:09:35.575 --> 00:09:38.373
I didn't mention this earlier.

00:09:38.444 --> 00:09:41.004
I didn't want to hurt
anybody's feelings...

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.570
but you are the one

00:09:42.648 --> 00:09:45.014
who people are most
looking forward to seeing.

00:09:45.084 --> 00:09:46.881
That's difficult to believe.

00:09:46.953 --> 00:09:47.885
Why?

00:09:47.954 --> 00:09:49.353
I was Borg.

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:50.855
Exactly.

00:09:50.923 --> 00:09:52.618
You were Borg,

00:09:52.692 --> 00:09:53.920
but you escaped.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:56.051
And despite incredible odds,

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:57.254
you managed to reclaim

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:59.389
your humanity.

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:00.659
No one's ever done that before.

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:01.665
You're famous.

00:10:01.734 --> 00:10:03.929
Fame is irrelevant.

00:10:04.003 --> 00:10:05.937
Maybe...

00:10:06.038 --> 00:10:07.630
but you've given hope

00:10:07.707 --> 00:10:10.175
to everyone who's ever
lost somebody to the Borg.

00:10:12.178 --> 00:10:14.510
You've inspired millions.

00:10:18.551 --> 00:10:21.714
If you think my participation
in the "hoopla"

00:10:21.787 --> 00:10:25.223
would be beneficial to others,
then I'll comply.

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:41.771
Is this going to take
much longer, Reg?

00:10:41.841 --> 00:10:44.275
Well, the computer is
still inputting data.

00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:45.970
That should do it.

00:10:46.078 --> 00:10:49.411
All right. Computer, display
the intended trajectory

00:10:49.482 --> 00:10:51.279
of the datastream transmitted

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.817
at 0600 this morning.

00:10:56.689 --> 00:10:58.316
Now, display
the actual trajectory

00:10:58.391 --> 00:11:00.086
and identify
the termination point.

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:03.060
The trajectory ends
in Sector 395...

00:11:03.129 --> 00:11:05.120
42, Grid 8.

00:11:06.599 --> 00:11:07.930
Does that sound familiar?

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.831
That's exactly
where the datastream

00:11:09.902 --> 00:11:11.096
dissipated last month.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.831
There is something there.

00:11:12.905 --> 00:11:14.930
There is something
preventing the datastream

00:11:15.007 --> 00:11:16.497
from reaching Voyager.

00:11:16.575 --> 00:11:19.408
Uh, a micro-wormhole,
a radiogenic field...

00:11:19.478 --> 00:11:20.638
Long-range scans

00:11:20.713 --> 00:11:22.146
didn't pick up
anything unusual.

00:11:22.214 --> 00:11:26.275
Well, still, we could send
a ship to investigate.

00:11:26.352 --> 00:11:27.842
We could confirm my theory.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.512
What about my theory, Reg?

00:11:29.588 --> 00:11:32.056
The hologram was too complex.

00:11:32.124 --> 00:11:33.682
It caused the data
streams to degrade

00:11:33.759 --> 00:11:35.386
before they reached
their destination.

00:11:35.461 --> 00:11:37.156
Well, to be honest...

00:11:37.229 --> 00:11:40.630
I... I don't agree.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:44.158
The truth is, we don't know
what happened to my hologram.

00:11:44.236 --> 00:11:46.830
Then let's stick
to what we do know.

00:11:46.906 --> 00:11:48.567
For the second
month in a row,

00:11:48.641 --> 00:11:50.700
we tried sending your
hologram to Voyager.

00:11:50.776 --> 00:11:52.243
And for the second
month in a row,

00:11:52.311 --> 00:11:53.335
it failed to get there.

00:11:53.412 --> 00:11:55.437
And I want to know why,
so it doesn't happen

00:11:55.514 --> 00:11:56.446
a third time.

00:11:56.515 --> 00:11:58.039
It won't happen a third time.

00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:02.347
Next month, we go back
to standard transmissions.

00:12:02.421 --> 00:12:04.912
But a holographic matrix
carries twice the information,

00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:06.581
interact with the crew...

00:12:06.659 --> 00:12:08.923
Admiral Paris wants us
to send more practical data,

00:12:09.028 --> 00:12:10.188
like tactical upgrades,

00:12:10.262 --> 00:12:11.695
letters from the
crew's families.

00:12:11.764 --> 00:12:13.288
But, Pete...

00:12:13.365 --> 00:12:15.731
Sending a hologram
to Voyager was a good idea,

00:12:15.801 --> 00:12:17.234
but it didn't work.

00:12:17.303 --> 00:12:20.363
It's time to move on.

00:12:26.946 --> 00:12:29.847
And this is the research lab,

00:12:29.915 --> 00:12:33.681
where most of Pathfinder's
homework gets done.

00:12:33.753 --> 00:12:36.381
All the datastreams
are compressed here

00:12:36.455 --> 00:12:37.683
and then transmitted

00:12:37.757 --> 00:12:39.725
all the way to
the Delta Quadrant.

00:12:39.792 --> 00:12:42.192
Your teacher tells me
you've been studying

00:12:42.261 --> 00:12:43.626
some of the Delta Quadrant races

00:12:43.696 --> 00:12:45.163
that Voyager
has described to us.

00:12:45.231 --> 00:12:46.698
Who can name one for me?

00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:48.324
The Talaxians.

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.526
Very good.

00:12:49.602 --> 00:12:50.626
The Ocampa.

00:12:50.703 --> 00:12:51.829
That's right. Who else?

00:12:51.904 --> 00:12:53.166
The Borg!

00:12:53.239 --> 00:12:54.228
The Borg!

00:12:54.306 --> 00:12:55.568
They assimilated my hologram.

00:12:55.641 --> 00:12:56.801
That's how it disappeared.

00:12:56.876 --> 00:12:57.808
Reg, now isn't the time.

00:12:57.877 --> 00:12:59.538
Look at this... last
month, a spacecraft

00:12:59.612 --> 00:13:01.876
passed within 20 meters
of the MIDAS Array,

00:13:01.947 --> 00:13:04.415
just hours before
we sent the first hologram.

00:13:04.483 --> 00:13:05.472
What is your point?

00:13:05.551 --> 00:13:06.779
20 meters.

00:13:06.852 --> 00:13:08.410
It's awfully close,
don't you think?

00:13:08.487 --> 00:13:09.146
Ensign.

00:13:09.221 --> 00:13:10.654
Look, the Borg must

00:13:10.723 --> 00:13:13.521
have sent a transwarp probe
to steal my hologram.

00:13:13.592 --> 00:13:16.288
Maybe because they, they thought
that it was carrying

00:13:16.362 --> 00:13:18.159
anti-Borg technology
to Voyager.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.857
It wasn't the Borg, Reg.

00:13:19.932 --> 00:13:22.662
Then it was the Romulans
using a cloaked ship.

00:13:22.735 --> 00:13:24.566
They've been curious
about Voyager for years...

00:13:24.637 --> 00:13:25.569
That is enough.

00:13:25.638 --> 00:13:26.730
But, you...

00:13:26.806 --> 00:13:28.103
I am sorry your idea

00:13:28.174 --> 00:13:29.698
didn't work,
but I can't have you

00:13:29.775 --> 00:13:31.174
going off on a tangent.

00:13:31.243 --> 00:13:32.642
Not again.

00:13:32.711 --> 00:13:35.874
You'll be no good
to Pathfinder or Voyager.

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:39.242
How much leave

00:13:39.318 --> 00:13:41.047
do you have saved up?

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.054
Not that much.

00:13:43.122 --> 00:13:45.955
50... maybe 60 days.

00:13:46.025 --> 00:13:47.356
Take a week, go home.

00:13:47.426 --> 00:13:48.358
Try to relax.

00:13:48.427 --> 00:13:49.257
But, Pete...

00:13:49.328 --> 00:13:50.693
No. That was not

00:13:50.763 --> 00:13:52.390
a request, Lieutenant.

00:13:56.535 --> 00:13:59.470
Maybe I'll go somewhere...

00:14:02.374 --> 00:14:03.773
take a vacation.

00:14:03.843 --> 00:14:06.778
Now that is the most
sensible thing

00:14:06.846 --> 00:14:09.110
I've heard you say all day.

00:14:09.181 --> 00:14:11.376
My cousin has
a beach house in Malaysia.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.577
She'd be happy
to lend it to you.

00:14:14.987 --> 00:14:21.085
Thanks, um, but I have
someplace else in mind.

00:14:29.702 --> 00:14:30.862
You, you wanted to see me?

00:14:30.936 --> 00:14:33.029
I've been going over
the instructions

00:14:33.105 --> 00:14:34.333
from Starfleet Medical.

00:14:34.406 --> 00:14:37.034
As far as I can tell,
their "new" inoculations

00:14:37.109 --> 00:14:38.303
aren't much different

00:14:38.377 --> 00:14:40.743
from run-of-the-mill
radiogenic vaccines.

00:14:40.813 --> 00:14:43.077
I don't think
they'll protect the crew.

00:14:43.148 --> 00:14:45.616
Did you try incorporating
a synthetic antigen?

00:14:45.684 --> 00:14:49.643
Yes, but it only improved
the resistance by 10 percent.

00:14:49.722 --> 00:14:51.280
That should be enough.

00:14:51.357 --> 00:14:53.917
We can't afford to
be cavalier, Reg.

00:14:53.993 --> 00:14:55.858
If these treatments
don't work,

00:14:55.928 --> 00:14:58.055
the crew will
wind up liquefied.

00:14:58.130 --> 00:14:59.859
You're forgetting
that the inoculations

00:14:59.932 --> 00:15:01.263
aren't designed to work alone.

00:15:01.333 --> 00:15:03.198
They were intended
to work in combination

00:15:03.269 --> 00:15:05.169
with the shield modifications.

00:15:05.237 --> 00:15:08.001
It's the medicinal "ying"
to the shields' "yang."

00:15:08.073 --> 00:15:10.098
A-and what if the "yang"
doesn't work?

00:15:10.175 --> 00:15:11.665
That's not going to happen.

00:15:11.744 --> 00:15:14.008
Now, listen,
Lieutenant Barclay

00:15:14.079 --> 00:15:16.912
has a special affinity
for this crew.

00:15:16.982 --> 00:15:18.472
So do I.

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:20.916
I promise you,
we won't let them down.

00:15:21.053 --> 00:15:23.487
Of course you won't.

00:15:23.555 --> 00:15:24.920
Tell me...

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:27.083
do you also share
Lieutenant Barclay's

00:15:27.159 --> 00:15:28.217
affinity for golf?

00:15:29.495 --> 00:15:31.122
We have identical handicaps.

00:15:31.196 --> 00:15:32.754
Well, if you're not busy later,

00:15:32.831 --> 00:15:35.391
perhaps we could play nine holes
on the holodeck.

00:15:35.467 --> 00:15:37.128
Eh, it's tempting,
but I still have

00:15:37.202 --> 00:15:39.534
a few dozen progress reports
to look over.

00:15:39.605 --> 00:15:40.833
Well, in that case,

00:15:40.906 --> 00:15:43.204
maybe you could
look over them here,

00:15:43.275 --> 00:15:46.039
so that I could borrow
the mobile emitter.

00:15:46.111 --> 00:15:48.375
Providing that the
rest of the day's work

00:15:48.447 --> 00:15:50.244
goes smoothly,
consider it yours.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:55.013
I... I thought it was mine.

00:15:56.221 --> 00:15:57.711
Commander Chakotay tells me

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:59.690
that you finished repairing
the transceiver.

00:15:59.758 --> 00:16:01.988
We were just about to send
the Captain's reply

00:16:02.061 --> 00:16:03.119
to Lieutenant Barclay.

00:16:03.195 --> 00:16:04.253
Do you have enough room

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:06.127
to include a progress
report from me?

00:16:06.198 --> 00:16:08.564
I think we can
squeeze that in.

00:16:08.634 --> 00:16:13.537
Computer, download
Barclay Hologram File 01

00:16:13.605 --> 00:16:15.698
to the data block.

00:16:15.774 --> 00:16:17.799
Download complete.

00:16:17.876 --> 00:16:19.605
Transmitting.

00:16:47.072 --> 00:16:50.337
It's about time.

00:16:50.409 --> 00:16:53.469
Greetings from
the Delta Quadrant, Lieutenant.

00:16:53.545 --> 00:16:54.512
You'll be happy to know

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:56.445
that your hologram
reached us safely...

00:16:56.515 --> 00:16:58.540
Get to the important part.

00:17:01.687 --> 00:17:04.178
In accordance with the
74th Rule of Acquisition...

00:17:04.256 --> 00:17:05.314
"Knowledge Equals Profit"

00:17:05.391 --> 00:17:08.554
I've enclosed the specifications
you've requested.

00:17:08.627 --> 00:17:10.458
See you soon.

00:17:10.529 --> 00:17:13.896
Oh, look at
those hands.

00:17:13.999 --> 00:17:16.160
I bet she gives
great oo-mox.

00:17:16.235 --> 00:17:18.328
Too bad she'll be dead
when she gets here.

00:17:18.404 --> 00:17:20.872
Forget the hands.

00:17:20.939 --> 00:17:22.634
Show me the nanoprobes.

00:17:26.045 --> 00:17:27.876
How many are there?

00:17:27.946 --> 00:17:29.538
3.6 million.

00:17:29.615 --> 00:17:33.176
That's 20 percent more
than we predicted.

00:17:33.252 --> 00:17:34.742
3.6 million nanoprobes

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:37.118
at six bars of latinum per unit.

00:17:37.189 --> 00:17:38.349
Uh, that comes to...

00:17:38.424 --> 00:17:41.882
More profit than
we ever dreamed of.

00:18:06.185 --> 00:18:08.153
Your drink, sir.

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:09.380
Thank you.

00:18:09.455 --> 00:18:11.423
Thank you.

00:18:19.898 --> 00:18:22.059
Something to drink, ma'am?

00:18:22.134 --> 00:18:23.601
I'm fine, thanks.

00:18:23.669 --> 00:18:24.863
Are you sure?

00:18:24.937 --> 00:18:26.529
I've got
a chocolate passion punch

00:18:26.605 --> 00:18:27.833
with your name on it.

00:18:29.007 --> 00:18:30.406
Reg?

00:18:30.476 --> 00:18:32.000
Surprise.

00:18:34.146 --> 00:18:35.841
Where's Commander Riker?

00:18:35.914 --> 00:18:37.779
He doesn't arrive until Friday.

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:39.112
Oh.

00:18:39.184 --> 00:18:41.175
The question is:
What are you doing here?

00:18:41.253 --> 00:18:43.016
Just had some time off.

00:18:43.088 --> 00:18:45.921
Your letter
made this place sound fun,

00:18:46.024 --> 00:18:48.049
and just thought I'd join you.

00:18:48.127 --> 00:18:50.925
Do you have any idea
how inappropriate it is

00:18:50.996 --> 00:18:53.362
to follow your therapist
on vacation?

00:18:53.432 --> 00:18:54.456
Please.

00:18:54.533 --> 00:18:57.058
They might be watching.

00:18:57.136 --> 00:18:58.467
Who?

00:18:58.537 --> 00:19:00.801
The Borg, the Romulans.

00:19:00.873 --> 00:19:02.500
I'm not sure yet.

00:19:02.574 --> 00:19:04.303
Please...

00:19:04.376 --> 00:19:07.675
Deanna, I need your help.

00:19:09.982 --> 00:19:12.314
Commander Harkins is usually
willing to hear me out,

00:19:12.384 --> 00:19:14.818
but this time, he wouldn't
even look at my evidence.

00:19:14.887 --> 00:19:17.754
I'm not sure any of this
qualifies as evidence, Reg.

00:19:17.823 --> 00:19:19.882
You don't believe me, either.

00:19:19.992 --> 00:19:22.187
You think I'm imagining this?

00:19:22.261 --> 00:19:23.455
Just like Pete?

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:27.389
The last time I saw you,

00:19:27.466 --> 00:19:31.027
you were laughing,
telling jokes.

00:19:31.103 --> 00:19:32.695
You even sang
a duet with Data.

00:19:34.206 --> 00:19:37.573
That was Commander La Forge's
birthday party.

00:19:37.643 --> 00:19:41.477
You were a completely
different Reg that night.

00:19:41.547 --> 00:19:42.878
Oh. Things were better then.

00:19:42.948 --> 00:19:43.915
How?

00:19:44.016 --> 00:19:45.074
Well, for one thing

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:46.708
I had just finished the matrix

00:19:46.785 --> 00:19:48.150
for my hologram,

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:50.882
and I showed Geordi
some of the specs that night.

00:19:50.956 --> 00:19:52.719
He said he was proud of me.

00:19:52.791 --> 00:19:53.917
What else?

00:19:54.059 --> 00:19:58.155
Oh... the Dragons had
just won the pennant,

00:19:58.230 --> 00:19:59.697
and I was

00:19:59.765 --> 00:20:02.928
still seeing Leosa.

00:20:03.068 --> 00:20:04.660
You mentioned her at the party.

00:20:04.736 --> 00:20:06.101
A teacher, right?

00:20:06.171 --> 00:20:07.433
Everything was going

00:20:07.506 --> 00:20:11.909
so well... my job,
my personal life.

00:20:11.977 --> 00:20:13.774
I started to think

00:20:13.845 --> 00:20:15.938
maybe my luck was changing.

00:20:16.081 --> 00:20:18.276
And then you lost your hologram.

00:20:23.021 --> 00:20:24.318
Admiral Paris was furious.

00:20:24.389 --> 00:20:26.857
He said we'd, we'd wasted
a transmission to Voyager.

00:20:26.925 --> 00:20:29.416
Pete talked him into
giving us another chance,

00:20:29.494 --> 00:20:31.758
but there was so much
pressure after that.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.923
Did it put a strain
on your relationship

00:20:33.999 --> 00:20:35.193
with Leosa?

00:20:35.267 --> 00:20:36.325
She left me.

00:20:36.401 --> 00:20:37.333
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:20:37.402 --> 00:20:38.562
I went to her apartment.

00:20:38.637 --> 00:20:39.797
She was gone.

00:20:39.871 --> 00:20:42.135
There was no furniture,
no forwarding address,

00:20:42.207 --> 00:20:43.697
not even a
"Dear Reg" letter.

00:20:43.775 --> 00:20:46.243
That must have been
very upsetting.

00:20:46.311 --> 00:20:47.972
Mmm. It's just
my luck, right?

00:20:48.113 --> 00:20:50.308
Lose the hologram
and the girl.

00:20:50.382 --> 00:20:51.644
Tell me more

00:20:51.717 --> 00:20:53.344
about Leosa.

00:20:53.418 --> 00:20:54.976
Oh. You would have liked her.

00:20:55.087 --> 00:20:57.783
She was sweet,
she was thoughtful

00:20:57.856 --> 00:20:59.824
and such
a wonderful listener.

00:20:59.891 --> 00:21:01.984
She would let me,
let me go on for hours.

00:21:03.061 --> 00:21:05.325
What did you
talk about?

00:21:05.397 --> 00:21:09.163
Oh. She was fascinated
by my work at Pathfinder

00:21:09.234 --> 00:21:11.259
and, uh...

00:21:11.336 --> 00:21:13.304
she didn't, uh...

00:21:14.473 --> 00:21:17.874
she didn't find
any of it boring.

00:21:17.943 --> 00:21:21.470
She made me feel interesting.

00:21:21.546 --> 00:21:24.606
What do you feel when
we talk about her now?

00:21:24.683 --> 00:21:29.347
Um, sadness, I suppose.

00:21:30.822 --> 00:21:32.653
A little confusion.

00:21:32.724 --> 00:21:35.249
I'm sensing something else...

00:21:36.795 --> 00:21:38.387
something beneath
the surface.

00:21:38.463 --> 00:21:39.623
What?

00:21:39.698 --> 00:21:41.791
I think you might
be sensing it, too.

00:21:41.867 --> 00:21:43.061
What?

00:21:43.135 --> 00:21:45.729
Suspicion, Reg.

00:21:45.804 --> 00:21:46.930
You suspect her of something.

00:21:47.005 --> 00:21:47.972
I suspect

00:21:48.073 --> 00:21:49.836
that she's happier without me,

00:21:49.908 --> 00:21:51.398
if that's what you mean.

00:21:51.476 --> 00:21:54.070
You think
Leosa had something to do

00:21:54.146 --> 00:21:56.444
with your disappearing hologram,

00:21:56.515 --> 00:21:58.983
but you can't bring yourself
to admit it.

00:21:59.084 --> 00:22:02.542
That's why you're projecting
your suspicions onto others.

00:22:02.621 --> 00:22:04.316
You're in denial.

00:22:05.791 --> 00:22:07.918
If there's any chance

00:22:08.026 --> 00:22:11.462
Leosa did breach
Pathfinder security,

00:22:11.530 --> 00:22:14.522
you need to tell
your superiors.

00:22:14.599 --> 00:22:16.863
I-I'd be humiliated... again.

00:22:18.637 --> 00:22:19.899
I'll go with you.

00:22:19.971 --> 00:22:22.269
What about your vacation?

00:22:22.341 --> 00:22:25.902
I'll be back here
before Will arrives.

00:22:25.977 --> 00:22:31.745
Do you really think
it's possible that Leosa

00:22:31.817 --> 00:22:33.944
stole my hologram?

00:22:34.052 --> 00:22:36.520
Why would she do that?

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:40.954
Maybe... maybe she wanted

00:22:41.093 --> 00:22:44.460
something to remember me by.

00:22:44.529 --> 00:22:46.724
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:22:46.798 --> 00:22:49.426
With the help
of the Barclay hologram,

00:22:49.501 --> 00:22:53.062
we've nearly completed
the modifications to Voyager.

00:22:53.138 --> 00:22:55.106
As for Reg, he's becoming

00:22:55.173 --> 00:22:57.471
extremely popular with the crew.

00:22:57.542 --> 00:22:59.339
Imagine my disappointment

00:22:59.411 --> 00:23:01.106
when I discovered
that Lieutenant Paris

00:23:01.179 --> 00:23:03.272
had eaten
all the scrambled eggs.

00:23:04.716 --> 00:23:07.276
It was pure,
unadulterated gluttony,

00:23:07.352 --> 00:23:10.549
gastronomic conduct
unbecoming a Starfleet officer.

00:23:10.622 --> 00:23:12.613
He knows
it's my favorite breakfast,

00:23:12.691 --> 00:23:14.056
but he ate them anyway.

00:23:14.126 --> 00:23:16.788
We have
an egg-mergency here, people.

00:23:16.862 --> 00:23:20.127
I want to know
what you plan to do about it.

00:23:20.198 --> 00:23:23.656
Maybe I can replicate
some more, Captain.

00:23:23.735 --> 00:23:25.498
Do it.

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:32.298
Thank you, thank you,
thank you, thank you.

00:23:32.377 --> 00:23:34.106
He's not only programmed
to get us home,

00:23:34.179 --> 00:23:35.510
he does impressions.

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:37.741
You see, it's always bothered
Lieutenant Barclay

00:23:37.816 --> 00:23:39.716
that he was uncomfortable
in large groups.

00:23:39.785 --> 00:23:43.744
So he designed me
to be the life of the party.

00:23:44.923 --> 00:23:46.083
I hope he's not too shy.

00:23:46.158 --> 00:23:47.785
He's going to have
150 new friends

00:23:47.859 --> 00:23:48.917
when we get back home.

00:23:48.994 --> 00:23:52.327
If we get home, Harry, if.

00:23:52.397 --> 00:23:53.591
Pardon my friend here.

00:23:53.665 --> 00:23:55.223
He's convinced we're destined

00:23:55.300 --> 00:23:57.700
to live out our days
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:23:57.769 --> 00:24:00.135
Your pessimism is illogical.

00:24:00.205 --> 00:24:02.196
Perhaps a mind-meld
would help to alleviate

00:24:02.274 --> 00:24:03.206
your concern.

00:24:04.509 --> 00:24:06.909
Sick Bay to Reg.

00:24:07.012 --> 00:24:09.276
Please report to Holodeck 2.

00:24:09.347 --> 00:24:10.336
On my way.

00:24:16.788 --> 00:24:20.087
I was starting to think
you'd forgotten our tee time.

00:24:20.158 --> 00:24:21.250
So, what'll it be?

00:24:21.326 --> 00:24:22.759
Pebble Beach at sunset?

00:24:22.828 --> 00:24:24.591
The back nine at Gedi Prime?

00:24:24.663 --> 00:24:25.823
Actually, Doctor...

00:24:25.897 --> 00:24:27.762
I'm afraid something's come up.

00:24:27.833 --> 00:24:30.165
I'm going to meet
with Seven of Nine.

00:24:30.235 --> 00:24:31.896
Oh, really?

00:24:31.970 --> 00:24:33.904
She's going to teach me
to play Kadis-Kot.

00:24:33.972 --> 00:24:34.939
Uh, Reg...

00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:36.507
when I agreed
to lend you my emitter,

00:24:36.575 --> 00:24:37.837
I did it
with the understanding

00:24:37.909 --> 00:24:40.241
that you needed it
for official business.

00:24:40.312 --> 00:24:41.609
What's your point?

00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:43.045
My point is that board games

00:24:43.114 --> 00:24:45.082
aren't exactly crucial
to your mission.

00:24:45.150 --> 00:24:48.881
And I suppose golf is?

00:24:48.954 --> 00:24:51.354
Reg...

00:24:54.159 --> 00:24:55.319
I'll tell you what.

00:24:55.393 --> 00:24:57.054
When we get back home,

00:24:57.128 --> 00:24:59.824
we'll play as much
golf as you like.

00:24:59.898 --> 00:25:02.332
Until then, let's
try to keep out

00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:03.992
of each other's hair.

00:25:04.069 --> 00:25:05.297
What do you say?

00:25:12.677 --> 00:25:14.201
State your name for the record.

00:25:14.279 --> 00:25:16.440
Leosa.

00:25:16.515 --> 00:25:18.346
L-e-o

00:25:18.416 --> 00:25:19.906
s-a.

00:25:20.051 --> 00:25:21.450
Occupation?

00:25:21.520 --> 00:25:23.283
Dabo girl.

00:25:23.355 --> 00:25:24.287
Dabo?

00:25:24.356 --> 00:25:25.687
It's a Ferengi game.

00:25:25.757 --> 00:25:28.749
I work aboard
one of their casino ships.

00:25:28.827 --> 00:25:31.159
You, you told me
you were a teacher.

00:25:31.229 --> 00:25:33.925
Is this true?

00:25:34.065 --> 00:25:36.499
Sometimes I'm a teacher.

00:25:36.568 --> 00:25:38.058
Sometimes I'm a Bajoran vedek.

00:25:39.704 --> 00:25:41.638
Whatever the customer wants.

00:25:41.706 --> 00:25:44.197
Lieutenant Barclay tells me
that the two of you

00:25:44.276 --> 00:25:46.904
have spent a significant amount
of time together.

00:25:46.978 --> 00:25:49.776
Did he ever discuss his work
at Pathfinder with you?

00:25:49.848 --> 00:25:52.544
Oh. Wouldn't talk
about anything else.

00:25:52.617 --> 00:25:55.177
It was always holograms this

00:25:55.253 --> 00:25:57.653
and cyclic pulsars that.

00:25:57.722 --> 00:26:00.384
And who did you share
that information with?

00:26:00.458 --> 00:26:02.722
Nobody.

00:26:02.794 --> 00:26:05.661
I have a theory.

00:26:05.730 --> 00:26:07.721
Would you like to hear it?

00:26:07.799 --> 00:26:10.666
Why not?

00:26:10.735 --> 00:26:12.327
I think that some
of your Ferengi friends

00:26:12.404 --> 00:26:14.565
found a way to profit
from Lieutenant Barclay's work.

00:26:14.639 --> 00:26:16.573
I think

00:26:16.641 --> 00:26:18.802
you were encouraged

00:26:18.877 --> 00:26:20.435
to get close to him,

00:26:20.512 --> 00:26:24.414
and when you had all
the information you needed,

00:26:24.482 --> 00:26:25.540
you left him.

00:26:25.617 --> 00:26:29.383
I left Reg
for one simple reason.

00:26:29.454 --> 00:26:31.251
He's boring.

00:26:37.062 --> 00:26:40.759
Don't tell me you never noticed.

00:26:40.832 --> 00:26:43.062
With the Admiral's permission,

00:26:43.134 --> 00:26:44.931
I'd like a moment alone

00:26:45.070 --> 00:26:46.435
with Leosa.

00:26:46.504 --> 00:26:48.404
I don't think therapy

00:26:48.473 --> 00:26:50.441
is what this woman needs,
Counselor.

00:26:50.508 --> 00:26:52.373
Five minutes, Admiral.

00:26:52.444 --> 00:26:55.641
Five minutes.

00:27:12.998 --> 00:27:16.126
Did you know I'm a Betazoid?

00:27:16.201 --> 00:27:17.691
I'm empathic,

00:27:17.769 --> 00:27:21.364
which means I know
when people are lying.

00:27:21.439 --> 00:27:23.771
Tell me, what's the longest

00:27:23.842 --> 00:27:26.504
you've ever been
incarcerated?

00:27:29.114 --> 00:27:31.810
You can't send me
to prison, Counselor.

00:27:31.883 --> 00:27:33.783
I didn't do anything wrong.

00:27:33.852 --> 00:27:37.219
Maybe not, but I can order you

00:27:37.288 --> 00:27:40.883
held for psychiatric
observation.

00:27:40.959 --> 00:27:43.427
Extended observation.

00:27:43.495 --> 00:27:46.589
I may not be a Betazoid

00:27:46.665 --> 00:27:48.792
but I work a dabo table,

00:27:48.867 --> 00:27:51.893
and I know
when somebody's bluffing.

00:27:55.707 --> 00:27:57.299
Try me.

00:28:05.050 --> 00:28:07.883
You were correct, Admiral.

00:28:07.986 --> 00:28:11.149
The Ferengi did steal
Reg's hologram... twice.

00:28:11.222 --> 00:28:12.348
This is the ship

00:28:12.424 --> 00:28:13.982
you need to look for.

00:28:24.069 --> 00:28:26.833
That's it.

00:28:26.905 --> 00:28:28.099
That's Nunk's ship.

00:28:30.875 --> 00:28:32.240
Nunk?

00:28:32.310 --> 00:28:35.404
My... employer.

00:28:35.480 --> 00:28:37.277
Scans indicate they've been
in the vicinity

00:28:37.348 --> 00:28:39.908
of that star
for the last 43 hours.

00:28:39.984 --> 00:28:41.576
Why?

00:28:41.653 --> 00:28:43.211
I don't know.

00:28:43.288 --> 00:28:45.552
She's telling the truth...

00:28:45.623 --> 00:28:47.181
for once.

00:28:47.258 --> 00:28:48.748
The Ferengi wouldn't
have stolen the hologram

00:28:48.827 --> 00:28:50.419
if they didn't think
it was valuable.

00:28:50.495 --> 00:28:54.363
They're probably waiting
to rendezvous with a buyer.

00:28:54.432 --> 00:28:57.060
Are there any Starfleet ships
in that area?

00:28:57.135 --> 00:28:59.365
The Carolina is
.7 light-years away.

00:28:59.437 --> 00:29:00.369
At maximum warp,

00:29:00.438 --> 00:29:01.632
it could reach them
in two hours.

00:29:01.706 --> 00:29:03.105
Open a channel.

00:29:04.809 --> 00:29:07.676
Computer, open a secure channel
to the Carolina.

00:29:07.746 --> 00:29:11.512
Tell Captain Peterson to adjust
his course immediately.

00:29:15.086 --> 00:29:18.886
Was everything that happened
between us a lie?

00:29:18.990 --> 00:29:20.321
Not everything.

00:29:20.391 --> 00:29:23.724
Just the parts where I
expressed affection for you.

00:29:25.830 --> 00:29:27.627
Oh...

00:29:27.699 --> 00:29:30.167
if it makes any difference,

00:29:30.235 --> 00:29:31.998
it wasn't personal.

00:29:32.070 --> 00:29:34.470
It was just... business.

00:29:34.539 --> 00:29:37.531
What exactly is a broken heart
worth these days, hmm?

00:29:38.610 --> 00:29:41.807
Ten percent.

00:29:41.880 --> 00:29:42.869
Of what?

00:29:42.947 --> 00:29:45.916
Profits from the nanoprobes.

00:29:45.984 --> 00:29:47.178
Nanoprobes?

00:29:47.252 --> 00:29:48.378
Mm-hmm.

00:29:48.453 --> 00:29:49.681
Borg nanoprobes?

00:29:49.754 --> 00:29:51.051
Yeah.

00:29:51.122 --> 00:29:52.749
Gegis says they're worth

00:29:52.824 --> 00:29:55.190
two billion times
their weight in latinum.

00:29:55.260 --> 00:29:57.694
Oh.

00:30:04.002 --> 00:30:04.934
I don't think

00:30:05.003 --> 00:30:06.436
I quite understand
the problem, Doctor.

00:30:06.504 --> 00:30:07.596
Are you aware

00:30:07.672 --> 00:30:09.264
that he's been doing
impressions of you?

00:30:09.340 --> 00:30:11.274
You should hear his
Tuvok... it's eerie.

00:30:11.342 --> 00:30:12.775
It's disrespectful.

00:30:12.844 --> 00:30:14.607
What do you want me
to do, deactivate him?

00:30:14.679 --> 00:30:16.772
Just long enough to run
a diagnostic of his program.

00:30:16.848 --> 00:30:18.110
His recent behavior

00:30:18.183 --> 00:30:19.844
may be indicative
of a more serious problem.

00:30:19.918 --> 00:30:21.476
I haven't seen
any evidence of that.

00:30:21.553 --> 00:30:22.485
Of course not.

00:30:22.554 --> 00:30:24.954
In front of you,
he's all smiles...

00:30:25.023 --> 00:30:29.551
but I've seen him
be rude and careless...

00:30:29.627 --> 00:30:31.959
two traits the real
Lieutenant Barclay

00:30:32.030 --> 00:30:33.292
never exhibited.

00:30:33.364 --> 00:30:35.389
I know the real Barclay
is a friend of yours,

00:30:35.466 --> 00:30:37.229
and I'm sorry
if the holographic version

00:30:37.302 --> 00:30:39.133
hasn't lived up
to your expectations,

00:30:39.204 --> 00:30:41.365
but that's hardly reason
to deactivate him.

00:30:41.439 --> 00:30:44.272
Are the lives of 150 crewmen
reason enough?

00:30:44.342 --> 00:30:45.639
Maybe you're right.

00:30:45.710 --> 00:30:47.473
Maybe I am overreacting,

00:30:47.545 --> 00:30:49.274
but what if I'm right?

00:30:49.347 --> 00:30:51.941
We're less than
a light-year away

00:30:52.016 --> 00:30:54.576
from the geodesic fold.

00:30:54.652 --> 00:30:58.144
Do you want to risk
being led through it

00:30:58.223 --> 00:31:00.589
by a malfunctioning hologram?

00:31:01.659 --> 00:31:03.422
Captain, you saved us
a com call.

00:31:03.494 --> 00:31:06.088
We're ready to bring the
enhanced shielding on line.

00:31:06.164 --> 00:31:07.597
Good work.

00:31:07.665 --> 00:31:10.099
I need a moment alone with Reg.

00:31:10.168 --> 00:31:12.102
Your program has been running
continuously

00:31:12.170 --> 00:31:13.603
for how many hours now?

00:31:13.671 --> 00:31:16.765
56 hours, 11 minutes
and 21 seconds.

00:31:16.841 --> 00:31:18.604
I'd like to run a
diagnostic of your matrix,

00:31:18.676 --> 00:31:20.644
make sure you haven't
suffered any degradation

00:31:20.712 --> 00:31:23.272
over the last few days.

00:31:23.348 --> 00:31:25.145
This isn't the, uh...

00:31:25.216 --> 00:31:26.945
Doctor's idea, is it?

00:31:27.085 --> 00:31:31.146
He expressed some concern
for your well-being, yes.

00:31:31.222 --> 00:31:32.951
I bet he did.

00:31:33.091 --> 00:31:34.524
Believe me, Reg, the crew and I

00:31:34.592 --> 00:31:36.253
are grateful
for everything you've done,

00:31:36.327 --> 00:31:37.954
but we need to take
every precaution.

00:31:38.029 --> 00:31:39.360
I understand perfectly.

00:31:39.430 --> 00:31:41.625
And if the ship's Doctor thinks

00:31:41.699 --> 00:31:44.133
I need a checkup,
who am I to argue?

00:32:03.321 --> 00:32:05.448
Why are you hiding
in the corner?

00:32:05.523 --> 00:32:07.514
I'm not hiding.

00:32:07.592 --> 00:32:11.358
I'm working on a way
to foil the Ferengi's plans.

00:32:11.429 --> 00:32:13.420
Reg, there's nothing
left to foil.

00:32:13.498 --> 00:32:16.160
The Carolina will have them
in custody within the hour.

00:32:16.234 --> 00:32:18.168
Leosa said the Ferengi

00:32:18.236 --> 00:32:21.535
were going to be selling
Borg nanoprobes.

00:32:21.606 --> 00:32:25.440
What does that have to do
with Voyager?

00:32:25.510 --> 00:32:27.137
They have a Borg crewman.

00:32:27.211 --> 00:32:28.803
Think about it.

00:32:28.880 --> 00:32:32.213
The Ferengi stole the original
Barclay hologram a month ago.

00:32:32.283 --> 00:32:34.410
That gave them time
to reprogram it

00:32:34.485 --> 00:32:36.476
and then smuggle it to Voyager

00:32:36.554 --> 00:32:37.953
in the next transmission.

00:32:38.056 --> 00:32:39.717
Reprogram it to do what?

00:32:39.791 --> 00:32:42.954
Steal Seven of Nine's
nanoprobes.

00:32:43.094 --> 00:32:45.892
For all we know, he could be

00:32:45.964 --> 00:32:48.296
dissecting her right now.

00:32:48.366 --> 00:32:52.393
What would the Ferengi want
with assimilation technology?

00:32:52.470 --> 00:32:55.098
Oh, nanoprobes aren't just
for assimilating.

00:32:55.173 --> 00:32:57.403
They can reanimate
necrotic tissue,

00:32:57.475 --> 00:32:59.534
slow down the aging process.

00:32:59.610 --> 00:33:02.078
They'd be priceless
for the Ferengi.

00:33:02.146 --> 00:33:04.307
Reg, even if the Ferengi

00:33:04.382 --> 00:33:08.546
did reprogram your hologram
to steal the nanoprobes,

00:33:08.619 --> 00:33:11.816
how would they get
their hands on them?

00:33:11.889 --> 00:33:14.722
Voyager's
30,000 light-years away.

00:33:14.792 --> 00:33:17.886
I haven't figured
that part out yet.

00:33:17.962 --> 00:33:22.524
Maybe they discovered a, a
wormhole or a subspace corridor.

00:33:24.836 --> 00:33:27.566
Have you mentioned any of this
to Commander Harkins?

00:33:27.638 --> 00:33:29.572
Not yet. I can't.

00:33:29.640 --> 00:33:32.609
If I don't bring him
hard evidence,

00:33:32.677 --> 00:33:35.942
he'll just think
that I'm fantasizing.

00:33:36.080 --> 00:33:40.744
For the time being, we need
to keep this between us.

00:33:48.326 --> 00:33:50.726
That tickles, Lieutenant.

00:33:50.795 --> 00:33:53.491
Sorry, Reg,
we're almost finished.

00:33:53.564 --> 00:33:55.464
Have you identified
any problems yet?

00:33:55.533 --> 00:33:57.228
I've gone over
his entire matrix.

00:33:57.301 --> 00:33:59.565
He's working perfectly.

00:33:59.637 --> 00:34:03.232
Maybe I'm not the one
who needs a diagnostic, hmm?

00:34:03.307 --> 00:34:06.743
I'm a big enough hologram
to admit when I'm wrong.

00:34:06.811 --> 00:34:08.836
I'm sorry I doubted you.

00:34:08.913 --> 00:34:11.074
Well, if anyone is owed
an apology, it's you.

00:34:11.149 --> 00:34:13.014
I should've been more sensitive.

00:34:13.084 --> 00:34:14.517
Friends?

00:34:14.585 --> 00:34:16.485
Friends.

00:34:16.554 --> 00:34:18.647
Now that that's out of the way,
Captain, what do you say

00:34:18.723 --> 00:34:20.281
we get this ship
back to Earth?

00:34:26.931 --> 00:34:28.421
It's time.

00:34:28.499 --> 00:34:31.627
Initiate the geodesic pulse.

00:34:45.216 --> 00:34:47.343
Would someone care to tell me

00:34:47.418 --> 00:34:49.249
what that is?

00:34:56.294 --> 00:34:58.387
It's a geodesic fold, Admiral.

00:34:58.463 --> 00:35:01.591
That's how they're going
to get the nanoprobes.

00:35:03.935 --> 00:35:06.369
Two million kilometers

00:35:06.437 --> 00:35:07.904
and closing, Captain.

00:35:07.972 --> 00:35:09.439
Take us to one-quarter impulse.

00:35:09.507 --> 00:35:10.906
Bridge to Astrometrics.

00:35:10.975 --> 00:35:12.806
Bring the enhanced
shielding on line.

00:35:12.877 --> 00:35:14.037
Aye, Commander.

00:35:15.446 --> 00:35:17.437
What's wrong?

00:35:19.984 --> 00:35:22.077
The fold contains
three radiation types

00:35:22.153 --> 00:35:23.711
we didn't account for.

00:35:23.788 --> 00:35:25.415
The shield modifications
are not enough.

00:35:25.490 --> 00:35:26.752
Well, the shields were modified

00:35:26.824 --> 00:35:28.758
to work in combination
with the inoculations.

00:35:28.826 --> 00:35:29.918
We'll be fine.

00:35:29.994 --> 00:35:31.256
If the shields fail,

00:35:31.329 --> 00:35:32.728
the inoculations
will be irrelevant.

00:35:32.797 --> 00:35:34.025
Astrometrics to the Bridge.

00:35:34.098 --> 00:35:34.860
Go ahead.

00:35:39.070 --> 00:35:40.537
What is it, Seven?

00:35:40.605 --> 00:35:44.336
There was a problem, Captain,

00:35:44.408 --> 00:35:46.467
but I've corrected it.

00:35:54.585 --> 00:35:58.214
I'm using the MIDAS Array to tap
into the Ferengi ship's sensors.

00:35:58.289 --> 00:36:00.780
They're receiving telemetry
through the fold.

00:36:00.858 --> 00:36:02.883
If I'm reading this correctly,
Voyager's headed right for it.

00:36:03.027 --> 00:36:04.255
Captain Janeway knows better

00:36:04.328 --> 00:36:05.295
than to take her ship

00:36:05.363 --> 00:36:06.728
into such a dangerous anomaly.

00:36:06.797 --> 00:36:10.324
If the Ferengi did alter
my hologram, then...

00:36:10.401 --> 00:36:12.198
it might... might be possible

00:36:12.270 --> 00:36:14.568
for him to have taken over
the ship.

00:36:14.639 --> 00:36:16.766
One hologram
against an entire crew?

00:36:16.841 --> 00:36:19.173
He may have found a way
to incapacitate the crew

00:36:19.243 --> 00:36:20.904
or to commandeer
the ship's systems,

00:36:21.045 --> 00:36:23.172
but either way, we've
got to get the Carolina

00:36:23.247 --> 00:36:24.236
to close the fold.

00:36:24.315 --> 00:36:26.249
The Carolina isn't
equipped to do that.

00:36:26.317 --> 00:36:27.909
Then they'll have to commandeer
the Ferengi ship

00:36:27.985 --> 00:36:28.917
and do it from there.

00:36:28.986 --> 00:36:30.044
The Carolina's still

00:36:30.121 --> 00:36:31.782
half a light-year away.
They won't make it in time.

00:36:31.856 --> 00:36:35.348
Can we transmit a message,
warn Voyager?

00:36:35.426 --> 00:36:38.418
Not through a geodesic fold.

00:36:44.535 --> 00:36:49.404
Our own starship,
with multiphasic shielding

00:36:49.473 --> 00:36:53.170
and a gold-pressed
latinum hull.

00:36:53.244 --> 00:36:55.940
We'll have enough left over
to buy a fleet of casino ships!

00:36:56.080 --> 00:37:00.141
I have a better idea...
lobe enlargements!

00:37:02.286 --> 00:37:03.514
Shh!

00:37:03.588 --> 00:37:04.748
Ooh, someone's
hailing us.

00:37:04.822 --> 00:37:06.255
Who?

00:37:06.324 --> 00:37:08.485
I can't tell.
There's too much interference.

00:37:08.559 --> 00:37:09.856
Answer it.

00:37:12.763 --> 00:37:14.025
It's the hologram.

00:37:14.098 --> 00:37:15.360
You said it was impossible

00:37:15.433 --> 00:37:17.367
to communicate
through the fold.

00:37:17.435 --> 00:37:18.902
I thought it was.

00:37:18.970 --> 00:37:20.835
I guess I did a better job

00:37:20.905 --> 00:37:23.271
of reprogramming the hologram
than I thought.

00:37:24.375 --> 00:37:25.433
We must close

00:37:25.509 --> 00:37:28.501
the geodesic fold immediately.

00:37:28.579 --> 00:37:31.013
Captain Janeway has
found out about our plan.

00:37:31.082 --> 00:37:32.549
If that's true,

00:37:32.617 --> 00:37:35.518
then why is she still
headed for the fold?

00:37:35.586 --> 00:37:37.577
Because she...

00:37:37.655 --> 00:37:40.920
found a way
to protect her ship.

00:37:41.025 --> 00:37:42.151
Impossible.

00:37:42.226 --> 00:37:43.887
You don't know Janeway.

00:37:43.961 --> 00:37:46.828
She's uncanny
when it comes to shields.

00:37:46.897 --> 00:37:48.296
She's furious.

00:37:48.366 --> 00:37:50.834
She said she was going to kill

00:37:50.901 --> 00:37:53.597
whoever tried to harm her crew.

00:37:53.671 --> 00:37:56.663
I strongly suggest
you abort the mission.

00:37:56.741 --> 00:37:58.800
What should we do?

00:37:58.876 --> 00:38:01.538
Go to warp before Janeway
makes it through.

00:38:01.612 --> 00:38:03.807
No, you mustn't!

00:38:03.881 --> 00:38:05.280
Voyager has
Borg interquadrental

00:38:05.349 --> 00:38:09.683
warp drives and...
Hirogen hunting sensors

00:38:09.754 --> 00:38:11.722
and Vidiian phase torpedoes.

00:38:11.789 --> 00:38:14.519
No matter where you run,
Voyager will find you.

00:38:14.592 --> 00:38:19.256
Your only hope...
is to close the fold.

00:38:27.705 --> 00:38:29.866
Harkins to Holodeck 1.

00:38:29.940 --> 00:38:31.532
Go ahead, Pete.

00:38:31.609 --> 00:38:33.804
It worked, Reg.

00:38:33.878 --> 00:38:35.709
They've started
to close the fold.

00:38:35.780 --> 00:38:37.407
Computer, end program.

00:38:41.986 --> 00:38:43.544
Something's wrong, Captain.

00:38:43.621 --> 00:38:45.782
Astrometrics to the Bridge.

00:38:45.856 --> 00:38:47.346
Why are we stopping?

00:38:47.425 --> 00:38:49.689
The fold's collapsing, Reg.

00:38:49.760 --> 00:38:51.250
We didn't make it in time.

00:38:51.329 --> 00:38:53.695
It's not too late
if we remodulate the shields.

00:38:53.764 --> 00:38:56.324
I appreciate your determination,
but we can't risk it.

00:38:56.400 --> 00:38:57.958
You did everything you could.

00:39:00.004 --> 00:39:01.904
Captain, someone just initiated

00:39:01.972 --> 00:39:03.439
a site-to-site transport.

00:39:03.507 --> 00:39:04.474
Who?

00:39:04.542 --> 00:39:06.009
Seven and Reg.

00:39:06.077 --> 00:39:07.305
They've beamed
to an escape pod.

00:39:07.378 --> 00:39:09.608
Bridge to Seven of Nine.
What's going on?

00:39:13.684 --> 00:39:14.651
The pod's been launched.

00:39:14.719 --> 00:39:16.243
Put a tractor beam on it.

00:39:18.923 --> 00:39:20.891
There is too much interference
from the fold.

00:39:21.025 --> 00:39:22.890
Harry, can you get
a transporter lock?

00:39:26.097 --> 00:39:27.530
What now?

00:39:27.598 --> 00:39:29.463
There's something coming
through the fold.

00:39:29.533 --> 00:39:30.465
Voyager?

00:39:30.534 --> 00:39:31.899
No, it's too small.

00:39:31.969 --> 00:39:33.095
A phase torpedo!

00:39:33.170 --> 00:39:34.694
Raise shields!

00:39:34.772 --> 00:39:36.706
Brace for impact!

00:39:43.280 --> 00:39:44.941
It's an escape pod.

00:39:50.154 --> 00:39:54.420
Maybe the hologram
sent us the drone.

00:39:54.492 --> 00:39:55.925
Ooh!

00:39:55.993 --> 00:39:57.858
Check what's in there.

00:39:59.296 --> 00:40:01.423
Nothing.

00:40:01.499 --> 00:40:06.402
No Borg corpse, no nanoprobes.

00:40:06.470 --> 00:40:08.700
No profit.

00:40:12.176 --> 00:40:14.371
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:40:14.445 --> 00:40:16.675
Seven of Nine
has recovered from her injuries

00:40:16.747 --> 00:40:18.942
and "Reg" has been deactivated.

00:40:19.016 --> 00:40:21.314
Until we finish
analyzing his program,

00:40:21.385 --> 00:40:23.785
his motivations
remain a mystery.

00:40:30.127 --> 00:40:32.652
Making first contact

00:40:32.730 --> 00:40:33.924
with a new life-form?

00:40:33.998 --> 00:40:35.397
"Mom's apple pie."

00:40:35.466 --> 00:40:38.094
Neelix thought
a little home cooking

00:40:38.169 --> 00:40:39.101
might cheer me up.

00:40:39.170 --> 00:40:39.966
And?

00:40:40.070 --> 00:40:41.799
I haven't worked up the courage

00:40:41.872 --> 00:40:42.839
to taste it yet.

00:40:42.907 --> 00:40:45.467
Have you figured out
what went wrong with Reg?

00:40:45.543 --> 00:40:48.876
Well, Seven thinks our proximity
to the fold degraded his matrix,

00:40:48.946 --> 00:40:51.141
but if you ask me,
it was a recursive error

00:40:51.215 --> 00:40:52.546
in his logic subroutine.

00:40:58.522 --> 00:41:00.149
Not bad...

00:41:00.224 --> 00:41:03.421
but it would have tasted better
in San Francisco.

00:41:06.363 --> 00:41:08.854
If it'll make you
feel any better,

00:41:08.933 --> 00:41:12.096
I'll let you in
on a little secret.

00:41:12.169 --> 00:41:14.228
I was on the Bridge
this morning

00:41:14.305 --> 00:41:17.035
when we received a hail
from an Iconian scientist.

00:41:17.107 --> 00:41:20.338
He claims to have a
transdimensional gateway

00:41:20.411 --> 00:41:22.606
that can take us
anywhere in the galaxy.

00:41:23.681 --> 00:41:25.911
I'm not that gullible.

00:41:25.983 --> 00:41:28.213
It's true. I was there.

00:41:28.285 --> 00:41:29.684
The Captain doesn't want us

00:41:29.753 --> 00:41:31.311
to get our hopes up,

00:41:31.388 --> 00:41:34.084
but personally, I think we'll
be home by the end of the week.

00:41:36.360 --> 00:41:38.851
Are you serious?

00:41:40.297 --> 00:41:42.697
You were right about him.

00:41:49.673 --> 00:41:54.372
Computer, install Barclay
Security Protocol 21-Alpha.

00:41:54.445 --> 00:41:57.209
Installation complete.

00:41:57.281 --> 00:42:00.148
Identify yourself.

00:42:00.217 --> 00:42:02.845
C-computer, deactivate
Barclay program.

00:42:04.321 --> 00:42:05.652
I'm sorry.

00:42:05.723 --> 00:42:06.917
I... I've been programming him

00:42:07.024 --> 00:42:09.015
with new security
precautions

00:42:09.093 --> 00:42:10.651
s-so he can't be stolen again.

00:42:10.728 --> 00:42:12.525
You seem to be off
to a good start.

00:42:12.596 --> 00:42:14.530
I thought you'd, uh,
be back at the beach.

00:42:14.598 --> 00:42:16.725
Will and I decided
to spend the rest

00:42:16.800 --> 00:42:18.461
of our vacation in Tiburon.

00:42:18.536 --> 00:42:19.468
We were wondering

00:42:19.537 --> 00:42:20.799
if you're free
for dinner tonight.

00:42:20.871 --> 00:42:23.271
Uh, I, oh...

00:42:23.340 --> 00:42:26.503
Oh, I, uh, I-I wouldn't want
to be a "third nacelle."

00:42:26.577 --> 00:42:27.669
Not possible.

00:42:27.745 --> 00:42:30.509
Will's bringing
a friend for you.

00:42:30.581 --> 00:42:32.310
Her name's Maril.

00:42:32.383 --> 00:42:34.248
You're going to adore her.

00:42:34.318 --> 00:42:37.685
I'd like to,
but I-I still have, uh...

00:42:37.755 --> 00:42:40.189
dozens of protocols to install.

00:42:40.257 --> 00:42:41.690
Maybe next time.

00:42:41.759 --> 00:42:44.284
Look, Reg,
I know Leosa hurt you,

00:42:44.361 --> 00:42:47.922
but hiding inside a hologrid
isn't the answer.

00:42:47.998 --> 00:42:51.161
You need to get out,
meet new people.

00:42:51.235 --> 00:42:54.466
This Maril wouldn't happen
to be a dabo girl

00:42:54.538 --> 00:42:55.869
by any chance?

00:42:55.940 --> 00:42:58.602
She's a teacher, actually...
a real one.

00:42:58.676 --> 00:42:59.700
Are you sure?

00:42:59.777 --> 00:43:00.869
Don't worry, Reg.

00:43:00.945 --> 00:43:04.073
We've taken
security precautions.
